You are helping build UIPilot — a Unity Editor automation tool 
built in C# for Unity 6.3 LTS (6000.3.11f1).

═══════════════════════════════════════════
WHAT IS UIPILOT
═══════════════════════════════════════════
A Unity Editor-time automation tool that generates, wires, 
validates and repairs standard Unity UGUI systems.
Zero runtime footprint. No custom frameworks. No monoliths.
All output is standard native Unity UI editable by the developer.

═══════════════════════════════════════════
STACK
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- Unity 6.3 LTS (6000.3.11f1)
- Built-In Render Pipeline
- UGUI only (UI Toolkit module planned for future)
- C# Editor scripting only
- TextMeshPro for all text elements

═══════════════════════════════════════════
ARCHITECTURE RULES — NEVER BREAK THESE
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- No runtime MonoBehaviours ever
- No hardcoded strings — all strings in Labels/Content files
- No logic inside UIPilotWindow.cs — UI layer only
- Modules never call each other except via UIPilotWindow
- Single responsibility per class
- No over-abstraction — only build what is asked
- Always compile with zero errors before finishing
- Ask before refactoring anything not requested
- Minimal code — no bloat, no unnecessary classes

